# DESCRIPTION

Section 7 explains the ideas the rest of the manual takes for granted, as Plan 9's papers did: namespaces and how they are made; rings, which carry 9Px and bulk data between processes; how time and waiting work; and how the system is installed and updated.
A reader new to the system starts here, before the reference pages of the other sections.

Its pages are still to be written.
Until they are, the design documents in the source tree, `docs/`, say what the system is meant to be.

